==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**5 [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**1 [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
**2 [[Fallen Bear]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You want to max up your cash and wallet before activating the boss wave. To do that, beat the first Dogenstein and Diabrollow to death with [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]. Afterwards Lutrinae Gokurakko will spawn. Use either [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and combine them with Can Can Cat or [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] to finish him off quickly because you will need more space to deal with the next wave of peons. This time though, you need to allow one of them to stay alive, or else your units will push fast into the base while you still haven't gotten any reasonable cash. The easiest way is to time [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to hit Diabrollow, then have it be knockbacked by Diabrallow which will let Bullet Train immediately hit him again, thus defeating him. Now you have a lone Dogenstein for a while, keep him up, and when a new Dogenstein comes, finish the current one with Bullet Train again.

When you reach maximum cash, start spamming all your slow meatshields and attackers, and once they reach halfway on the battleground, start spamming your fast units too. If you want to rush/[[cheese]], you might consider spamming the fast attackers earlier but keep them at bay just for a while using Dogenstein, since one respawns around every 40 seconds, infinitely. After hitting the base, time [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] to destroy both of the Fallen Bears that appear on the boss wave, and if that happens to not work, try timing [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]]. Afterwards, send [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to deal with the Fallen Bear who has no shield.

To deal with Lutrinae Gokurakko and Mini Angel Cyclone on boss wave, full-spam these certain units: Manic Eraser Cat, Ramen Cat, Cafeteria Cat/[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], Can Can Cat, Bullet Train Cat and any other unit you think that might help, fast, cheap with good DPS, but for Mini Angel Cyclone, be careful, try making it get a few heavy hits instead of multiple light hits, because she has many KBs which will often disrupt your units, Though that contradicts the usage of Ramen Cat because he is the main reason why Mini Angel Cyclone gets knockbacked that often and considering how powerful his pushing is, you better try to deal with her as soon as possible, and not allow Cruel Angel Clionel get anywhere near the base, because then you will still be left with one or even two of the Fallen Bears still alive, and their push to your base is inevitable.

